    {
      "title": "List of video games considered the best",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "\n\n{{DR case status|failed}}\n{{drn filing editor|Andrzejbanas|00:45, 11 January 2026 (UTC)}}\n{{DRN archive top|Closed as failed.  Excessively lengthy discussion was unable to narrow the issues down to a limited number of alternatives.  A [[WP:RFC|Request for Comments]] with a large number of alternatives was then launched, but the responses were that the RFC would not be constructive, and the RFC is being cancelled.  It is clear that several editors are dissatisfied with the current methodology, but they have provided long statements that are too verbose to be a useful basis for formulating an RFC.  Resume discussion on the article talk page.  A new request can be made for discussion here leading to the formulation of a new RFC if the discussion identifies no more than two alternatives.  [[User:Robert McClenon|Robert McClenon]] ([[User talk:Robert McClenon|talk]]) 17:42, 14 February 2026 (UTC)}}\n<span style=\"font-size:110%\">'''Have you discussed this on a talk page?'''</span>\n\nYes, I have discussed this issue on a talk page already.\n\n<span style=\"font-size:110%\">'''Location of dispute'''</span>\n* {{pagelinks|List of video games considered the best}}\n<span style=\"font-size:110%\">'''Users involved'''</span>\n* {{User|Andrzejbanas}}\n* {{User|Pro translator}}\n* {{User|NegativeMP1}}\n* {{User|TompaDompa}}\n* {{User|Phediuk}}\n* {{User|Rollinginhisgrave}}\n* {{User|SnowFire}}\n* {{User|Shooterwalker}}\n<span style=\"font-size:110%\">'''Dispute overview'''</span>\n\nA discussion that initially involved suggesting changing the past \"List of video games considered the best\" to \"List of video games voted the best\". From there, the conversation has been expanded to the list being against various guidelines. The ones brought up were [[WP:LISTCRITERIA]] (\" Avoid original or arbitrary criteria that would synthesize a list that is not plainly verifiable in reliable sources.\"), [[WP:INTERPRETING]] (on how the data is interpreted to clarify \"considered the best\" games). Further discussion has come as discussion went further on clarify that if what \"best\" is meant to be, as sources put different figures on this or if even using the term \"best\" is appropriate here per [[MOS:WTW]]. All the editors can not seem to agree if the current format is following the guidelines or not.\n\n<span style=\"font-size:110%\">'''How have you tried to resolve this dispute before coming here?'''</span>\n\n[[Talk:List of video games considered the best#Changing title to \"List of video games voted the best\"]]\n\n<span style=\"font-size:110%\">'''How do you think we can help resolve the dispute?'''</span>\n\nThe discussion has come to us sort of continuously replying or re-iterating points to hope and convince each other. It's gotten to a point where it's unclear on what points we are all at and how to analyze rules and guidelines. Mediation on where we currently stand and fresh guidance to help us get our points across would help us move forward with how to handle the article.\n{{collapse top|Discussion taking place at [[Wikipedia:Dispute resolution noticeboard/List of video games]].  [[User:Robert McClenon|Robert McClenon]] ([[User talk:Robert McClenon|talk]]) 03:00, 22 January 2026 (UTC)}}\n",
